  "body": "What happens: #3631 adds `operation::pocket_fit_advice`. The MCP replies show its warning when a 2D Pocket's tool has no position in the region that Generate cuts. The operation page in the UI does not show this warning yet.\n\nWhy it is separate: the UI display advice is cached by the frame-cost rule (`crates/ui/AGENTS.md`, #2238). The advice calls `collect_job` and slices the model. It must not run on each frame. The UI needs a cache in `crates/ui/src/height_memo.rs` (or a sibling) with a key of the inputs: the operation params, the tool diameter, the area controls, the source, and the geometry revision. It also needs a counter test and a changed-input test.\n\nExpected: the operation page shows the same sentence as the MCP `warning` when the advice returns `Some`. A still frame computes nothing again.\n\nDone means: a UI test shows the sentence for a 10 mm tool on an 8 x 8 mm Inside stock pocket, and no sentence for the Outside containment. A counter test shows that a still frame does not build the advice again.\n",
